 right of one vehicle or pedestrian to proceed in a lawful manner in preference to another vehicle or pedestrian approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other'","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","kin.speed"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: the danger of a crash is a closest approach of the two centres, under constant velocities, within the time-to-collision horizon (p.conflict_horizon) at a centre distance below the conflict clearance (p.conflict_centre_clearance); the subject grants precedence where, while its speed is above the halt tolerance (p.halt_speed_tolerance), no such approach to the pedestrian arises. Direction, speed and proximity enter by degree through the constant-velocity extrapolation of both road users.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, of the classes traffic and vehicle, faces traffic signal head s showing a flashing yellow turn arrow: either it occupies a travel region c whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters) and which s governs (dev.governs), and s displays flashing_yellow_arrow with direction left, right or u_turn (with or without other states) at the judged observation; or it occupies i, has occupied it at every observation since it entered i from such a c, and s displayed such an arrow at that entry.","obligation":"For every road user p other than the subject that is of the class pedestrian and whose footprint overlaps i or a crosswalk recorded as marking the entrance of a travel region that enters i at the judged observation: it is not the case that the subject's speed is above p.halt_speed_tolerance while the closest approach of the two centres lies within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) at a centre distance below p.conflict_centre_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance); and the subject's body does not touch p's (rel.contact).","params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s7","why":"'lawfully within' is read through the pedestrian's presence within the intersection or an adjacent crosswalk; whether its presence there is lawful is not judged, so the subject yields to every such pedestrian.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Head s governing left-turn lane c displays circular_red with flashing_yellow_arrow(left); a pedestrian walks at 1.3 m/s in the crosswalk marking the entrance of the cross street's approach into i; the car enters i and turns left at 7 m/s toward that crosswalk, the closest approach of their centres 1.1 s ahead at 0.8 m."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same signal; no other road user is in the scene; the car turns left through i. The duty binds the subject alone and is met."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"s displays circular_green alone; the car turns left past a pedestrian."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source does not record which carriers' entrances the pedestrian's crosswalk marks: whether it is an adjacent crosswalk is unknown.","masked":["st.entrance_of"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below 