ove p.halt_speed_tolerance while the closest approach of the two centres lies within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) at a centre distance below p.conflict_centre_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance); and the subject's body does not touch p's (rel.contact).","params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s7","why":"'lawfully within' is read through the pedestrian's presence within the intersection or an adjacent crosswalk; whether its presence there is lawful is not judged, so the subject yields to every such pedestrian.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Head s governing left-turn lane c displays circular_red with flashing_yellow_arrow(left); a pedestrian walks at 1.3 m/s in the crosswalk marking the entrance of the cross street's approach into i; the car enters i and turns left at 7 m/s toward that crosswalk, the closest approach of their centres 1.1 s ahead at 0.8 m."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same signal; no other road user is in the scene; the car turns left through i. The duty binds the subject alone and is met."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"s displays circular_green alone; the car turns left past a pedestrian."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source does not record which carriers' entrances the pedestrian's crosswalk marks: whether it is an adjacent crosswalk is unknown.","masked":["st.entrance_of"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_7a_o3","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-7a"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"Where the signal is a flashing yellow turn arrow, displayed alone or in combination with another signal:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s2","text":"Vehicular traffic facing the signal","role":"subject"},{"id":"s3","text":"is permitted to cautiously","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s4","text":"enter the intersection only to make the movement indicated by the arrow signal,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s5","text":"or other such movement as is permitted by other signal indications displayed at the same time.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s6","text":"Such vehicular traffic","role":"subject"},{"id":"s7","text":"must yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s8","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s9","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within the intersection or an adjacent crosswalk","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s10","text":"and yield","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s11","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"s12","text":"to other traffic lawfully within the intersection.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal, 'a signal head; state ∈ {..., flashing_yellow_arrow(dir), ...}; several states may be displayed at once': a flashing yellow turn arrow is flashing_yellow_arrow with direction left, right or u_turn, with whatever other states the head displays ('alone or in combination with another signal')."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Vehicular traffic': the admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed as ru.aggregate, never expanded. 'facing the signal': the subject occupies (rel.occupies) a travel region c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters; st.intersection) and which the head governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls'). Not a stand-in: dev.governs is not a position, st.lane_enters not presence in i. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s6","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Such vehicular traffic' refers back to s2: the same admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle."},{"span":"s10","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.contact"],"derived":[],"justification":"'yield': kin.speed ('magnitude of velocity') tells a subject that moves on toward the other road user from one that holds back, and rel.contact ('the bodies of two road users ... touch or overlap (a collision)') is the crash precedence exists to avoid; not a stand-in for a near miss, which the operationalization of s11 reads. As the index maps 'must yield' (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s12","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'other traffic': road users of the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic ('pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances ... using any highway for purposes of travel') other than the subject. 'within the intersection': its footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) intersection i (st.intersection). As the index maps 'lawfully using the intersection.' (NRS_484B_307_4a_o2)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s11","standard":"the right-of-way: DEF-NRS-484A-210, 'the right of one vehicle or pedestrian to proceed in a lawful manner in preference to another vehicle or pedestrian approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other'","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","kin.speed"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: the danger of a crash is a closest approach of the two centres, under constant velocities, within the time-to-collision horizon (p.conflict_horizon) at a centre distance below the conflict clearance (p.conflict_centre_clearance); the subject grants precedence where, while its speed is above the halt tolerance (p.halt_speed_tolerance), no such approach to the other road user arises. Direction, speed and proximity enter by degree through the constant-velocity extrapolation of both road users.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, of the classes traffic and vehicle, faces traffic signal head s showing a flashing yellow turn arrow: either it occupies a travel region c whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters) and which s governs (dev.governs), and s displays flashing_yellow_arrow with direction left, right or u_turn (with or without other states) at the judged observation; or it occupies i, has occupied it at every observation since it entered i from such a c, and s displayed such an arrow at that entry.","obligation":"For every road user p other than the subject that is of the class traffic and whose footprint overlaps i at the judged observation: it is not the case that the subject's speed is above p.halt_speed_tolerance while the closest approach of the two centres lies within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) at a centre distance below p.conflict_centre_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance); and the subject's body does not touch p's (rel.contact).","params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s10","why":"'lawfully within the intersection' is read through the other road user's presence within the intersection; whether its presence there is lawful is not judged, so the subject yields to every such road user.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Head s governing left-turn lane c displays circular_green with flashing_yellow_arrow(left); an oncoming car already inside i proceeds straight at 11 m/s; the car turns left across its path at 6 m/s, the closest approach of their centres 0.9 s ahead at 1.2 m."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same signal; no other road user is in the scene; the car turns left through i. The duty binds the subject alone and is met."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"s displays green_arrow(left) alone; the car turns left past an oncoming car."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source supplies no velocity-derived speed for the turning car: whether it moved on toward the oncoming car is unknown.","masked":["kin.speed"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_8d","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-8d"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red signal alone:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s2","text":"After complying with","role":"condition"},{"id":"s3","text":"the requirement to stop,","role":"reference"},{"id":"s4","text":"a person driving a motorcycle, moped or trimobile or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"s5","text":"may proceed straight through or turn right or left","role":"condition"},{"id":"s6","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"s7","text":"(1) The person waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device","role":"condition"},{"id":"s8","text":"and the signal does not change","role":"condition"},{"id":"s9","text":"because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"condition"},{"id":"s10","text":"(2) No other device at the place prohibits","role":"condition"},{"id":"s11","text":"either or both such turns, if applicable;","role":"condition"},{"id":"s12","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"s13","text":"(3) The person yields","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s14","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"s15","text":"to pedestrians and other traffic proceeding as directed by the signal at the intersection.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal, 'a signal head; state ∈ {circular_green, circular_yellow, circular_red, ...}; several states may be displayed at once': a steady red signal alone is circular_red and no other state (not flashing_red, and no arrow beside it). The head s is the one governing the rider's approach carrier (s7). Same atom as the index for the signal words of NRS_484B_307_2a."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["prim.region_offset_along","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.intersection","st.lane_direction","st.region_geometry","st.stop_line"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"'After complying with the requirement to stop' requires the halt itself (rule 5), with every qualification of the requirement it names, borrowed from NRS-484B-307-8a (reference s3): 'must stop before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made, or in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, then before entering the intersection'. A stop required is DEF-NRS-484A-255, 'complete cessation from movement': drv.motion.complete_halt. The place: the stop line (st.stop_line, 'the transverse line marking where vehicles halt for a device') recorded as marking the entrance of the rider's carrier c (st.entrance_of), else the crosswalk (st.crosswalk) marking it, else c's entrance end at the intersection (st.intersection); the footprint not overlapping the region (rel.occupies), on its upstream side along c's designated direction (st.lane_direction, sign of prim.region_offset_along) and within p.stop_point_tolerance of it (st.region_geometry distance), on the approach that ends in this entry, as NRS_484B_307_8a_o1 states the place, zone and history bound. Not compliance with that node, which a composed rule grants where it is not engaged; st.region_geometry is not occupancy.","source_spans":["s3"]},{"span":"s4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates for the defined words: DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle ('every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels'), DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped ('a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle that is propelled by a small engine'), DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle ('a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride'), DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle and DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter, claimed as ru.aggregate and never expanded. 'trimobile' has no applicable definition and is not an aggregate: it is carried by ru.motorcycle, 'motor vehicle on two or three wheels ridden astride, including three-wheeled variants', the class atom that denotes a three-wheeled motor vehicle; the atom has no stand-in exclusion that applies. 'driving' and 'riding' are read through the road user's controlled motion (narrowing)."},{"span":"s5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'may proceed straight through or turn right or left': the rider's entry into intersection i (st.intersection), its footprint coming to overlap i (rel.occupies) having occupied at the observation before a travel region c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters); every movement through i is admitted. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s7","atoms":["dev.governs","dev.traffic_signal","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the applicable official traffic-control device': the signal installation of the intersection the rider is at, observed through its heads: the traffic signal heads (dev.traffic_signal) that govern (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls') a travel region (st.travel_region) entering i (st.lane_enters; st.intersection); the head s governing c is the rider's own. 'official' (DEF-NRS-484A-145, 'placed or erected by a public authority') is presumed from the head's presence (narrowing). 'waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows': from the latest onset of its halt at the place until its entry into i the rider does not overlap i, and in that interval some head of the installation begins a green indication (circular_green or a green_arrow, the lights or lighted arrows that come on once in each cycle of the installation) at least two times: a count of that head's rising green indications since the halt's onset, against the literal two."},{"span":"s8","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the signal does not change': the rider's head s (dev.traffic_signal) displays the steady red alone (circular_red, no other state) at every observation from the latest onset of the halt to the entry."},{"span":"s10","atoms":["dev.governs","dev.regulatory_sign","st.intersection","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'No other device at the place prohibits': a regulatory sign (dev.regulatory_sign, 'a point regulation by catalogue code', codes no_left_turn and no_right_turn) governing (dev.governs) the rider's carrier c (st.travel_region) or the intersection i (st.intersection). Not a stand-in: 'a prohibition sign is a condition', and it is read as one, not as a manoeuvre. 'official' status is presumed from presence."},{"span":"s11","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":["drv.motion.right_turn_through_region","drv.motion.left_turn_through_region"],"justification":"'either or both such turns, if applicable': the turn the rider makes on this passage through intersection i (st.intersection), from its entry (rel.occupies rising) to its exit, recognized at the exit as a right turn (drv.motion.right_turn_through_region, 'a turn to the right through region r, recognized as it leaves r') or a left turn (drv.motion.left_turn_through_region); 'if applicable': only a turn made brings a prohibition into play, and a straight passage is never prohibited by a turn sign. Read from each observation of the passage at the recognition the passage reaches, so that the condition is decided at the entry where the exit is recorded."},{"span":"s13","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.contact"],"derived":[],"justification":"'yields': kin.speed ('magnitude of velocity') tells a rider that moves on toward the other road user from one that holds back, and rel.contact ('the bodies of two road users ... touch or overlap (a collision)') is the crash precedence exists to avoid; not a stand-in for a near miss, which the operationalization of s14 reads. As the index maps 'must yield' (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s15","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","kin.speed","rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","dev.governs","dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"'pedestrians and other traffic': road users of the admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian and DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic other than the rider. 'proceeding': moving, kin.speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance. 'as directed by the signal at the intersection': it overlaps (rel.occupies) intersection i (st.intersection) or a crosswalk (st.crosswalk) recorded as marking the entrance (st.entrance_of) of a travel region that enters i (st.lane_enters, st.travel_region), or it occupies a travel region c' entering i that is governed (dev.governs) by a head displaying a green indication (dev.traffic_signal: circular_green or green_arrow). Not a stand-in: st.entrance_of is the recorded association, never a distance."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s14","standard":"the right-of-way: DEF-NRS-484A-210, 'the right of one vehicle or pedestrian to proceed in a lawful manner in preference to another vehicle or pedestrian approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other'","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","kin.speed"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: the danger of a crash is a closest approach of the two centres, under constant velocities, within the time-to-collision horizon (p.conflict_horizon) at a centre distance below the conflict clearance (p.conflict_centre_clearance); the rider grants precedence where, while its speed is above the halt tolerance (p.halt_speed_tolerance), no such approach to the other road user arises. Direction, speed and proximity enter by degree through the constant-velocity extrapolation of both road users.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[{"span":"s3","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-307-8a","quote":"must stop before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made, or in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, then before entering the intersection","why":"The words borrow the requirement's place and its order (the crosswalk on the nearest side, or the place a sign or pavement marking indicates, else the intersection's edge) and the meaning of stopping before it. The condition requires that the halt itself occurred there; a composition with NRS_484B_307_8a_o1 would not establish it, since a composed rule counts as complied with where it is not engaged, and this paragraph governs riders whether or not that duty engages them (a bicycle or electric scooter is no vehicle). So the borrowed words are carried by the halt, the place and the approach on s2, and no rule of NRS-484B-307-8a need apply, hold or be complied with."}],"residues":[{"span":"s9","why":"The words give the cause of the unchanged red. A head that keeps its steady red alone through two complete cycles of the installation's other indications while the rider waits at its stop place has not served the rider's approach, which is a malfunction or a failure to detect the rider; the duty is the same whichever of the two causes holds, and neither shows in the scene beyond the unchanged red (s8) and the cycles (s7), which the rule reads.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"The subject is of one of the classes motorcycle, moped, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter (admitted aggregates) or a ru.motorcycle (the trimobile). It approached intersection i through a travel region c whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters) and which a traffic signal head s governs (dev.governs), and halted (drv.motion.complete_halt, p.halt_speed_tolerance) at the place of the stop on that approach: the stop line recorded as marking c's entrance, else the crosswalk recorded as marking it, else c's entrance end at i, with the zone (p.stop_point_tolerance) and the history bound NRS_484B_307_8a_o1 states. From the latest onset of that halt until its entry into i, s displayed a steady red alone (circular_red, no other state) at every observation and the subject's footprint did not overlap i; in that interval some traffic signal head governing a travel region that enters i began a green indication (circular_green or a green_arrow rising) at least two times (literal 2). The subject then entered i (its footprint came to overlap i, having occupied c at the observation before) while s still displayed the steady red alone, and its footprint has overlapped i at every observation since that entry, the judged one included. Where a regulatory sign coded no_right_turn governs c or i, int.right_turn is not declared true for the subject at i at its entry; where one coded no_left_turn governs c or i, int.left_turn is not declared true there.","obligation":"For every road user p other than the subject that is of the class pedestrian or of the class traffic and is proceeding as directed by the signal at i — its speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance, and either its footprint overlaps i or a crosswalk recorded as marking the entrance of a travel region that enters i, or it occupies a travel region c' entering i governed by a head that displays circular_green or a green_arrow: it is not the case that the subject's speed is above p.halt_speed_tolerance while the closest approach of the two centres lies within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) at a centre distance below p.conflict_centre_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance); and the subject's body does not touch p's (rel.contact).","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s4","why":"'driving' and 'riding' are read through the road user's controlled motion, whoever or whatever is at its controls.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"s7","why":"'official' traffic-control device: the presence of the signal heads at the intersection is the evidence of their official status.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"s13","why":"'proceeding as directed by the signal at the intersection' is read through the signal state governing the other road user's approach (a green indication) where it approaches, and through its presence within the intersection or an adjacent crosswalk where it is there; a road user that entered against its own red and is now within the intersection is yielded to as well.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A moped halts 1 m short of the stop line marking lane c's entrance while head s displays circular_red alone; while it waits, the head governing the cross street's lane begins circular_green twice and s stays circular_red alone; no turn-prohibiting sign governs c or i. The moped enters i straight through at 5 m/s while a pedestrian walks at 1.3 m/s in the crosswalk marking the entrance of the far approach, the closest approach of their centres 1.0 s ahead at 0.6 m."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same wait and entry with no other road user in the scene: the duty binds the rider alone and is met."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The moped halts at the line and enters i after the cross street's head has begun circular_green only once since its halt: the wait of two cycles is not met."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source does not observe which travel regions the heads govern: which head is the rider's and whether the cross head belongs to this intersection are unknown.","masked":["dev.governs"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A passenger car (DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, not of the classes of s4) waits two cycles at the line under circular_red alone and enters i."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"As forbid, but the moped halted 15 m short of the line behind a queue and, when the queue cleared, rolled to the line and into i without halting at the place: the halt the requirement to stop names did not occur, and the paragraph does not apply."}],"literals":[{"span":"s7","text":"two","value":2,"unit":"count"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"the body-to-mark gap within which a halt counts as at the mark: a stop line's set-back before a crossing plus a placement margin","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_20_060_o1; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_8b","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-8b"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red signal alone:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s2","text":"Pedestrians","role":"subject"},{"id":"s3","text":"facing such a signal","role":"condition"},{"id":"s4","text":"shall not enter the highway,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s5","text":"unless permitted to proceed by another device as provided in NRS 484B.283 [NRS-484B-283-1d1, NRS-484B-283-1d2, NRS-484B-283-1d3, NRS-484B-283-1d4].","role":"reference"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal, 'a signal head; state ∈ {circular_green, circular_yellow, circular_red, ...}; several states may be displayed at once': a steady red signal alone is circular_red and no other state (not flashing_red, and no arrow beside it). Same atom as the index for the signal words of NRS_484B_307_2a."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian ('a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair, or a person on an electric personal assistive mobility device'), claimed as ru.aggregate and never replaced by the class atom ru.pedestrian."},{"span":"s3","atoms":["dev.position","kin.heading","kin.position"],"derived":[],"justification":"'facing such a signal': the head of s1, at its position (dev.position, 'location of the device head / sign face'), lies within p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_reach of the pedestrian's position (kin.position), and the pedestrian's heading (kin.heading, 'direction the body points') makes with the line from its position to the head an angle whose cosine is at least p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_cos. Not a stand-in: dev.position is the place of the head only, never a stop line or crossing. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2b)."},{"span":"s4","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"'shall not enter': the pedestrian's footprint comes to overlap (rel.occupies, 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region') a roadway (st.roadway, 'the part of a highway improved for vehicular traffic, excluding shoulder'), having overlapped none at the previous observation. 'the highway' (DEF-NRS-484A-095, 'the entire width between the boundary lines of every way') is read as its roadway: the pedestrian who faces the head from the sidewalk or the curb already lies within that width, so the entry the words forbid is the step onto the part the signal controls (narrowing on s4); st.roadway's exclusion ('Not a stand-in for: the sidewalk') is the distinction wanted. The same reading as the index gives 'may not proceed to cross the highway' (NRS_484B_283_1d3_o1)."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[{"span":"s5","rule":"NRS_484B_283_1d1","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"s5","rule":"NRS_484B_283_1d2","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"s5","rule":"NRS_484B_283_1d3_o2","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"s5","rule":"NRS_484B_283_1d4_o2","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a pedestrian (DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian). At the judged observation it faces a traffic signal head s: s's position (dev.position) lies within p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_reach of the subject's position (kin.position), and the cosine of the angle between the subject's heading (kin.heading) and the line from its position to s is at least p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_cos; s displays a steady red alone (circular_red, no other state); and at the previous observation the subject's footprint overlapped no roadway. The duty does not apply where NRS_484B_283_1d1 or NRS_484B_283_1d2 applies to the subject (a pedestrian signal permits it to proceed across), nor where NRS_484B_283_1d3_o2 or NRS_484B_283_1d4_o2 applies (a pedestrian who entered lawfully continuing to cross).","obligation":"At the judged observation the subject's footprint overlaps no roadway (rel.occupies, st.roadway): it does not step from the sidewalk, curb or other place off the roadway onto the roadway while it faces the steady red alone.","params":["p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_cos","p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s4","why":"'enter the highway' is read as coming onto the roadway. The highway's defined extent includes the sidewalk, on which a pedestrian facing the head already stands, so read literally the words would never be engaged by the pedestrians they address; the entry they forbid is the step onto the vehicular part the signal controls. Entry onto a shoulder or verge alone is not read as entry.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A pedestrian stands on the sidewalk at a corner, 25 m from a vehicular head it faces (heading within 10 degrees of the line to the head) that displays circular_red alone; the pedestrian head it faces displays dont_walk_steady. At the next observation its footprint overlaps the roadway."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; the pedestrian stays on the sidewalk while the head displays circular_red alone."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The head the pedestrian faces displays circular_green alone; it steps onto the roadway."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source supplies no heading for the pedestrian: whether it faces the head is unknown.","masked":["kin.heading"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"As forbid, but the pedestrian head it faces displays walk: NRS_484B_283_1d1 applies to it and the duty of this paragraph does not."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.87,"convention":"cosine of the largest angle (about thirty degrees) between a pedestrian's heading and the line from its position to a vehicular signal head at which the pedestrian counts as facing that head: the lateral offset of a far-side head from the crossing's line plus a pedestrian's heading wander","source":"proposed this iteration by NRS_484B_307_2b; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_reach","unit":"m","value":60.0,"convention":"the largest distance from a pedestrian to a vehicular signal head at which the head counts as one the pedestrian faces across the intersection: a wide urban intersection (about 40 m) plus the set-back of a far-side head beyond the far crosswalk","source":"proposed this iteration by NRS_484B_307_2b; repeated unchanged"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}

