{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_8a_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-8a"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red signal alone:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s2","text":"Vehicular traffic facing the signal","role":"subject"},{"id":"s3","text":"must stop before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made, or in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, then before entering the intersection,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s4","text":"and,","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"s5","text":"except as otherwise provided in paragraphs (c) and (d) [(c) is appended below, NRS-484B-307-8d],","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s6","text":"must remain stopped or standing until the green signal is shown.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s7","text":"After complying with the requirement to stop,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s8","text":"vehicular traffic facing such a signal and situated on the extreme right of the highway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s9","text":"may proceed into the intersection","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s10","text":"for a right turn","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s11","text":"only when the intersecting highway is two-directional or one-way to the right,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s12","text":"or vehicular traffic facing such a signal and situated on the extreme left of a one-way highway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s13","text":"may proceed into the intersection","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s14","text":"for a left turn","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s15","text":"only when the intersecting highway is one-way to the left,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s16","text":"but must yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s17","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s18","text":"to pedestrians and other traffic proceeding as directed by the signal at the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal, 'a signal head; state ∈ {circular_green, circular_yellow, circular_red, ...}; several states may be displayed at once': a steady red signal alone is circular_red and no other state (not flashing_red, and no arrow beside it). Same atom as the index for the signal words of NRS_484B_307_2a."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Vehicular traffic': the admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle ('every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway'), claimed as ru.aggregate, never expanded. 'facing the signal': the subject occupies (rel.occupies) a travel region c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters; st.intersection) and which the head governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls'). Not a stand-in: dev.governs is not the place of the halt, st.lane_enters not presence in i. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s3","atoms":["prim.region_offset_along","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.intersection","st.lane_direction","st.region_geometry","st.stop_line"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"'must stop': a stop required, DEF-NRS-484A-255, '\"Stop,\" when required, means complete cessation from movement': drv.motion.complete_halt. 'before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection': the crosswalk (st.crosswalk, 'marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection') recorded as marking the entrance of the subject's carrier c (st.entrance_of, 'the line or crossing a vehicle approaching through that carrier halts at or before'); 'where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made': the stop line (st.stop_line, 'the transverse line marking where vehicles halt for a device') recorded as marking c's entrance; 'or in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, then before entering the intersection': c's entrance end at intersection i (st.intersection). 'before entering': the footprint does not yet overlap the region (rel.occupies); the side is read by the sign of prim.region_offset_along along c's designated direction (st.lane_direction), the distance to the place by st.region_geometry ('the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it'). Not a stand-in: st.region_geometry is not occupancy, and prim.region_offset_along is read for the side only, never as the distance. Same mapping as the index for the stop words of NRS_484A_450_2 and NRS_484A_450_3."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, of the classes traffic and vehicle, enters intersection i at the judged observation: its footprint overlaps i (rel.occupies) there and did not at the previous observation, at which it occupied a travel region c whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters) and which a traffic signal head s governs (dev.governs); and s displays at the judged observation a steady red alone (circular_red and no other state).","obligation":"Rule 4c duty: an act at a place before an event. Event: the entry into i just described; each such entry is its own occurrence. Place: the stop line recorded as marking c's entrance (st.entrance_of) where one is; else the crosswalk recorded as marking c's entrance; else c's entrance end at the edge of i. Where a mark's association with c is not observed, whether it governs is unknown; where its list of entrances is observed and excludes c, it does not govern and the next place in that order is read. Act: a complete halt (drv.motion.complete_halt, speed_tol = p.halt_speed_tolerance) at an observation at which the subject occupies c, its footprint overlaps neither i nor the crosswalk marking c's entrance and it is not past the stop line where one is the place, it lies on the upstream side of the place along c's designated direction (st.lane_direction; the sign of prim.region_offset_along shows the place ahead, or zero on the line), and its body is within p.stop_point_tolerance of the place (st.region_geometry distance). History bound: the search runs back from the entry and ends at the approach start, the last observation before the entry at which the subject, on c, is outside the place's stopping zone upstream (off the place, short of it, and farther from it than p.stop_point_tolerance), or at the subject's previous entry into i from c, whichever is later; nothing else ends it: not the start of the recording, not the subject's first observation, not another intersection or mark, not a distance travelled. Only an observed exit from the zone upstream begins a new approach; a creep, a lateral move or a change of lane within the zone keeps a halt already made. A halt found: complied. Either end reached without a halt: violated. Neither end reached and no halt found (the recording begins with the subject inside the zone): unknown. Whether the entry occurred is unknown where the observation before does not show the subject on a mapped carrier whose association with the place is observed, or where there is no observation before.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s3","why":"The place 'where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made' is read as the stop line the source records as marking the approach's entrance: a sign standing without a line indicates a place the ontology does not record (no regulatory sign code marks a stopping point), so where only such a sign indicates the place the duty is read at the crosswalk or the intersection's edge. The places are read in the order stop line, crosswalk, edge of the intersection, a halt before the first that marks the approach meeting the words for all of them.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car occupies lane c, recorded as entering i and governed by head s displaying circular_red alone; a stop line marks c's entrance. The car passes the line at 12 m/s, its speed never at or below the halt tolerance, and its footprint comes to overlap i while s still displays circular_red alone; the search from the entry reaches the approach start (the car 40 m short of the line) without a halt."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same approach; the car halts with its body 1 m short of the stop line, footprint off the line and the crosswalk, waits, and then enters i for a right turn while s still displays circular_red alone: the halt lies within the approach."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The car enters i while s displays circular_green alone."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source supplies no speed for the car at any observation of the approach: whether it halted is unknown.","masked":["kin.speed"]},{"name":"history_boundary","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The recording begins with the car already on c with its body 1.5 m short of the stop line, moving at 1 m/s; it enters i under circular_red alone without halting in the recording. The approach start and any earlier entry lie before the recording, so neither end of the search is reached.","boundary":"the car's approach on c before it came within the stop-point tolerance of the stop line"},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"No stop line or crosswalk marks c's entrance (every line's and crosswalk's list of entrances is observed and excludes c); the car halts with its body 1 m short of the edge of i and then enters i under circular_red alone: the place is the intersection's edge."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"the body-to-mark gap within which a halt counts as at the mark: a stop line's set-back before a crossing plus a placement margin","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_20_060_o1; repeated unchanged"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_8a_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-8a"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red signal alone:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s2","text":"Vehicular traffic facing the signal","role":"subject"},{"id":"s3","text":"must stop before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made, or in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, then before entering the intersection,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s4","text":"and,","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"s5","text":"except as otherwise provided in paragraphs (c) and (d) [(c) is appended below, NRS-484B-307-8d],","role":"reference"},{"id":"s6","text":"must remain stopped or standing until the green signal is shown.","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s7","text":"After complying with the requirement to stop,","role":"exception"},{"id":"s8","text":"vehicular traffic facing such a signal and situated on the extreme right of the highway","role":"exception"},{"id":"s9","text":"may proceed into the intersection","role":"exception"},{"id":"s10","text":"for a right turn","role":"exception"},{"id":"s11","text":"only when the intersecting highway is two-directional or one-way to the right,","role":"exception"},{"id":"s12","text":"or vehicular traffic facing such a signal and situated on the extreme left of a one-way highway","role":"exception"},{"id":"s13","text":"may proceed into the intersection","role":"exception"},{"id":"s14","text":"for a left turn","role":"exception"},{"id":"s15","text":"only when the intersecting highway is one-way to the left,","role":"exception"},{"id":"s16","text":"but must yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s17","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s18","text":"to pedestrians and other traffic proceeding as directed by the signal at the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal, 'a signal head; state ∈ {circular_green, circular_yellow, circular_red, ...}; several states may be displayed at once': a steady red signal alone is circular_red and no other state (not flashing_red, and no arrow beside it). Same atom as the index for the signal words of NRS_484B_307_2a."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Vehicular traffic': the admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed as ru.aggregate, never expanded. 'facing the signal': the subject occupies (rel.occupies) a travel region c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters; st.intersection) and which the head governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls'). Not a stand-in: dev.governs is not a position, st.lane_enters not presence in i. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s6","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'remain stopped or standing' (DEF-NRS-484A-255, 'complete cessation from movement'; DEF-NRS-484A-250, 'the halting of a vehicle ... otherwise than for the purpose of and while actually engaged in receiving or discharging passengers') at the place of the stop: the subject's footprint does not come to overlap (rel.occupies) the crosswalk recorded as marking c's entrance (st.crosswalk, st.entrance_of) nor intersection i (st.intersection). 'until the green signal is shown': the duty holds while the head (dev.traffic_signal) displays the steady red alone and ends once it displays another state. Not a stand-in: st.entrance_of is the recorded association, never a distance."},{"span":"s7","atoms":["prim.region_offset_along","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.intersection","st.lane_direction","st.region_geometry","st.stop_line"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"'After complying with the requirement to stop' refers to s3 of this line and requires the halt itself with every qualification s3 states: 'must stop before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made, or in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, then before entering the intersection'. A complete halt (drv.motion.complete_halt; DEF-NRS-484A-255, 'complete cessation from movement') at that place — the stop line (st.stop_line) recorded as marking c's entrance (st.entrance_of), else the crosswalk (st.crosswalk) marking it, else c's entrance end at i (st.intersection) — with the footprint not overlapping the region (rel.occupies), on its upstream side along c's direction (st.lane_direction, sign of prim.region_offset_along) and within p.stop_point_tolerance of it (st.region_geometry), on the approach that ends in this entry: the place, zone and history bound of NRS_484B_307_8a_o1. The halt itself, not compliance with that node, which a composed rule grants where it is not engaged."},{"span":"s8","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency","st.lane_enters"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicular traffic': the admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle. 'facing such a signal': the steady red head governs (dev.governs) the carrier c the subject occupies (rel.occupies), whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters). 'situated on the extreme right of the highway': c is a lane (st.lane, 'a longitudinal strip of roadway for one line of vehicles') whose ordinal equals the count of lanes in its direction (st.lane_adjacency, 'lane ordinal within the carriageway and the count of lanes in that direction; ordinal 1 is the leftmost lane'): the rightmost lane. Not a stand-in: lane membership is read from the ordinal, never from a lateral offset ('lane membership is not an offset from the edge')."},{"span":"s9","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'may proceed into the intersection': the subject's entry into intersection i (st.intersection), its footprint coming to overlap i (rel.occupies) having occupied at the observation before the travel region c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters); the place at which the intention of s10 is declared. As the index maps 'may proceed straight through or turn right or left' (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s11","atoms":["st.highway","st.on_way","st.intersection","st.lane","st.lane_direction","st.median_or_divider"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the intersecting highway': each highway region (st.highway, 'the entire public way between its boundary lines') that i lies on (st.on_way, 'an intersection lies on every way that meets there') other than a highway c lies on. 'two-directional' (DEF-NRS-484B-073, 'an undivided highway upon which vehicles are allowed to proceed in opposite directions'): no median or dividing section (st.median_or_divider, 'physical barrier or dividing section between roadways') lies on it, and two lanes (st.lane) lying on it carry designated directions (st.lane_direction) whose cosine is below minus p.lane_opposed_direction_cos. 'one-way to the right': at least one lane lies on it and every lane lying on it carries a designated direction to the right of c's designated direction, the cross product of c's direction with the lane's (d_x times l_y minus d_y times l_x) being below minus p.cross_direction_sin_min. Not a stand-in: st.on_way is the way a region lies on, not nearness; st.lane_direction is local to its carrier."},{"span":"s12","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency","st.lane_enters","st.one_way_roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicular traffic facing such a signal': as s8. 'situated on the extreme left': c is a lane (st.lane) of ordinal 1 (st.lane_adjacency, 'ordinal 1 is the leftmost lane'); 'of a one-way highway': the subject's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a one-way roadway (st.one_way_roadway, 'roadway on which traffic is restricted to one direction'), as the index maps 'Upon a highway designated and signposted for one-way traffic' (NRS_484B_220_1). Not a stand-in: lane membership is read from the ordinal, never from an offset."},{"span":"s13","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"As s9: the subject's entry into i from c (rel.occupies rising; st.lane_enters; st.travel_region; st.intersection), the place at which the intention of s14 is declared."},{"span":"s15","atoms":["st.highway","st.on_way","st.intersection","st.lane","st.lane_direction"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the intersecting highway': each highway region (st.highway) that i lies on (st.on_way) other than a highway c lies on. 'one-way to the left': at least one lane (st.lane) lies on it and every lane lying on it carries a designated direction (st.lane_direction) to the left of c's designated direction, the cross product of c's direction with the lane's being above p.cross_direction_sin_min. Not a stand-in: st.on_way is not nearness."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[{"span":"s10","id":"int.right_turn"},{"span":"s14","id":"int.left_turn"}],"compositions":[{"span":"s5","rule":"NRS_484B_307_8d","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, of the classes traffic and vehicle, occupies at the judged observation, or occupied at the previous one, a travel region c whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters) and which a traffic signal head s governs (dev.governs); s displays a steady red alone (circular_red, no other state) at the judged observation; and at the previous observation the subject's footprint overlapped neither i nor a crosswalk recorded as marking c's entrance (st.entrance_of). Exception (paragraph (c), appended in this line, s7 to s15): at the judged observation the subject's footprint overlaps i, it has halted at the place of the stop on this approach (the place, zone and history bound of NRS_484B_307_8a_o1), and either (right) c is a lane whose ordinal equals the count of lanes in its direction, int.right_turn is declared true for the subject at i, and every highway i lies on other than one c lies on is two-directional (no median or divider lies on it; two lanes on it with directions opposed within p.lane_opposed_direction_cos) or one-way to the right (every lane on it points to the right of c's direction by more than p.cross_direction_sin_min); or (left) c is a lane of ordinal 1, the subject's footprint overlaps a one-way roadway, int.left_turn is declared true for the subject at i, and every such highway is one-way to the left. Exception (paragraph (d), s5): NRS_484B_307_8d applies to the subject.","obligation":"At the judged observation the subject's footprint overlaps neither i nor a crosswalk recorded as marking c's entrance (rel.occupies): having stopped, or still short of the place, it remains short of them while the steady red alone is displayed; once s displays another state (the green shown) the duty no longer applies.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance","p.lane_opposed_direction_cos","p.cross_direction_sin_min"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s6","why":"'remain stopped or standing' is read at the place the stop was due: the subject leaves the stop when its footprint comes to overlap the crosswalk marking its carrier's entrance or the intersection while the steady red alone is displayed. A movement short of them, such as closing up behind a vehicle ahead before reaching the place or a creep within the stop-point zone, is not read as leaving the stop: the stop the words require is the one at the place.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car halts at the stop line of lane c (ordinal 2 of 3), which enters i and is governed by head s displaying circular_red alone; int.right_turn is not declared; 5 s later it moves off and its footprint comes to overlap the crosswalk marking c's entrance while s still displays circular_red alone."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The car halts at the line under circular_red alone and stays short of the crosswalk until s displays circular_green; it then enters i."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"s displays circular_green alone throughout the car's approach and entry."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source does not observe which travel regions s governs: whether the car faces s is unknown.","masked":["dev.governs"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The car halts with its body 1 m short of the stop line in the rightmost lane (ordinal 3 of 3), int.right_turn is declared for it at i, and the cross street is undivided with lanes in both directions; it enters i under circular_red alone: paragraph (c)'s exception holds."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"As branch_1, but the cross street is one-way and every lane on it points to the car's left: the exception does not hold, and the entry under the red violates."},{"name":"branch_3","expected":"violated","narrative":"As branch_1, but the car halted 15 m short of the line behind a queue and, when the queue cleared, rolled to the line and into i without halting at the place: the halt the exception refers to did not occur."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"the body-to-mark gap within which a halt counts as at the mark: a stop line's set-back before a crossing plus a placement margin","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_20_060_o1; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.lane_opposed_direction_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.9,"convention":"cosine of the largest angle (about twenty-five degrees) off exactly opposed at which the designated directions of two mapped lanes of one way count as opposite directions of travel: the direction noise of map lane segments along a gently curving way","source":"map lane-direction tolerance, matching the catalogue's tolerance for opposed vehicle headings (p.oncoming_heading_cos)"},{"name":"p.cross_direction_sin_min","unit":"ratio","value":0.5,"convention":"sine of the smallest angle (thirty degrees) by which a way's designated direction lies to one side of an approach's designated direction for that way's traffic to count as flowing to that side: the legs of a junction meet at larger angles, and map direction noise is far smaller","source":"intersection design guidance limiting the skew of junction legs"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}

