d-in: st.on_way is the way a region lies on, not nearness; st.lane_direction is local to its carrier."},{"span":"s8","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency","st.lane_enters","st.one_way_roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicular traffic facing such a signal': as s4. 'situated on the extreme left': c is a lane (st.lane) of ordinal 1 (st.lane_adjacency, 'ordinal 1 is the leftmost lane'); 'of a one-way highway': the subject's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a one-way roadway (st.one_way_roadway, 'roadway on which traffic is restricted to one direction'), as the index maps 'Upon a highway designated and signposted for one-way traffic' (NRS_484B_220_1). Not a stand-in: lane membership is read from the ordinal, never from an offset."},{"span":"s9","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"As s5: the subject's entry into i from c (rel.occupies rising; st.lane_enters; st.travel_region; st.intersection), the place at which the intention of s10 is declared."},{"span":"s11","atoms":["st.highway","st.on_way","st.intersection","st.lane","st.lane_direction"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the intersecting highway': each highway region (st.highway) that i lies on (st.on_way) other than a highway c lies on. 'one-way to the left': at least one lane (st.lane) lies on it and every lane lying on it carries a designated direction (st.lane_direction) to the left of c's designated direction, the cross product of c's direction with the lane's being above p.cross_direction_sin_min. Not a stand-in: st.on_way is not nearness."},{"span":"s12","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.contact"],"derived":[],"justification":"'must yield': kin.speed ('magnitude of velocity') tells a subject that moves on toward the other road user from one that holds back, and rel.contact ('the bodies of two road users ... touch or overlap (a collision)') is the crash precedence exists to avoid; not a stand-in for a near miss, which the operationalization of s13 reads. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s14","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","kin.speed","rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","dev.governs","dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"'pedestrians and other traffic': road users of the admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian and DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic other than the subject. 'proceeding': moving, kin.speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance. 'as directed by the signal at the intersection': it overlaps (rel.occupies) intersection i (st.intersection) or a crosswalk (st.crosswalk) recorded as marking the entrance (st.entrance_of) of a travel region that enters i (st.lane_enters, st.travel_region), or it occupies a travel region c' entering i that is governed (dev.governs) by a head displaying a green indication (dev.traffic_signal: circular_green or green_arrow). Not a stand-in: st.entrance_of is the recorded association, never a distance."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s13","standard":"the right-of-way: DEF-NRS-484A-210, 'the right of one vehicle or pedestrian to proceed in a lawful manner in preference to another vehicle or pedestrian approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other'","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","kin.speed"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: the danger of a crash is a closest approach of the two centres, under constant velocities, within the time-to-collision horizon (p.conflict_horizon) at a centre distance below the conflict clearance (p.conflict_centre_clearance); the subject grants precedence where, while its speed is above the halt tolerance (p.halt_speed_tolerance), no such approach to the other road user arises. Direction, speed and proximity enter by degree through the constant-velocity extrapolation of both road users.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[{"span":"s6","id":"int.right_turn"},{"span":"s10","id":"int.left_turn"}],"compositions":[{"span":"s3","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-307-8a","quote":"must stop before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made, or in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, then before entering the intersection","why":"The words borrow the requirement's place and its order (the crosswalk on the nearest side, or the place a sign or pavement marking indicates, else the intersection's edge) and the meaning of stopping before it. The condition requires that the halt itself occurred there; a composition with NRS_484B_307_8a_o1 would not establish it, since a composed rule counts as complied with where it is not engaged. So the borrowed words are carried by the halt, the place and the approach on s2, and no rule of NRS-484B-307-8a need apply, hold or be complied with."}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, of the classes traffic and vehicle, approached intersection i through a travel region c whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters) and which a traffic signal head s governs (dev.governs), and entered i (its footprint came to overlap i, having occupied c and not i at the observation before) at an observation at which s displayed a steady red alone (circular_red, no other state), after halting at the place of the stop on that approach (s2 with s3: the place, zone and history bound NRS_484B_307_8a_o1 states); at that entry either (right) c is a lane whose ordinal equals the count of lanes in its direction, int.right_turn is declared true for the subject at i, and every highway i lies on other than one c lies on is two-directional (no median or divider lies on it; two lanes on it with directions opposed within p.lane_opposed_direction_cos) or one-way to the right (every lane on it points to the right of c's direction by more than p.cross_direction_sin_min); or (left) c is a lane of ordinal 1, the subject's footprint overlaps a one-way roadway, int.left_turn is declared true for the subject at i, and every such highway is one-way to the left. Its footprint has overlapped i at every observation since that entry, the judged one included.","obligation":"For every road user p other than the subject that is of the class pedestrian or of the class traffic and is proceeding as directed by the signal at i — its speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance, and either its footprint overlaps i or a crosswalk recorded as marking the entrance of a travel region that enters i, or it occupies a travel region c' entering i governed by a head that displays circular_green or a green_arrow: it is not the case that the subject's speed is above p.halt_speed_tolerance while the closest approach of the two centres lies within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) at a centre distance below p.conflict_centre_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance); and the subject's body does not touch p's (rel.contact).","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance","p.lane_opposed_direction_cos","p.cross_direction_sin_min","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s12","why":"'proceeding as directed by the signal at the intersection' is read through the signal state governing the other road user's approach (a green indication) where it approaches, and through its presence within the intersection or an adjacent crosswalk where it is there; a road user that entered against its own red and is now within the intersection is yielded to as well.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car halts with its body 1 m short of the stop line of the rightmost lane c (ordinal 2 of 2), int.right_turn declared at i, the cross street undivided with lanes in both directions; it enters i under circular_red alone at 4 m/s while a car on the cross street, on a lane entering i governed by a head displaying circular_green, approaches from the left at 12 m/s, the closest approach of their centres 1.5 s ahead at 1 m."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The same right turn on red with no other road user in the scene: the duty binds the subject alone and is met."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The car halts in lane c and enters i only after s displays circular_green alone."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but lane ordinals and counts are not observed: whether the car is on the extreme right is unknown (c is on no one-way roadway, so the left branch is decided false).","masked":["st.lane_adjacency"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"As forbid, but the car halted 15 m short of the stop line behind a queue and rolled into i without halting at the place: the halt the words require did not occur and the duty of this paragraph does not arise."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car halts at the stop line of the leftmost lane (ordinal 1) of a one-way roadway, int.left_turn declared at i, every lane of the cross street pointing to its left; it enters i under circular_red alone at 5 m/s while a pedestrian walking at 1.3 m/s in the crosswalk marking the entrance of a cross-street lane into i is closing on its path, the closest approach of their centres 1.2 s ahead at 0.7 m."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"the body-to-mark gap within which a halt counts as at the mark: a stop line's set-back before a crossing plus a placement margin","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_20_060_o1; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.lane_opposed_direction_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.9,"convention":"cosine of the largest angle (about twenty-five degrees) off exactly opposed at which the designated directions of two mapped lanes of one way count as opposite directions of travel: the direction noise of map lane segments along a gently curving way","source":"map lane-direction tolerance, matching the catalogue's tolerance for opposed vehicle headings (p.oncoming_heading_cos)"},{"name":"p.cross_direction_sin_min","unit":"ratio","value":0.5,"convention":"sine of the smallest angle (thirty degrees) by which a way's designated direction lies to one side of an approach's designated direction for that way's traffic to count as flowing to that side: the legs of a junction meet at larger angles, and map direction noise is far smaller","source":"intersection design guidance limiting the skew of junction legs"},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}

