{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_6a","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-6a"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"Where the signal is a steady yellow signal alone:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s2","text":"Vehicular traffic facing the signal","role":"subject"},{"id":"s3","text":"is thereby warned that the related green movement is being terminated or that a steady red indication will be exhibited immediately thereafter,","role":"definitional"},{"id":"s4","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"s5","text":"such vehicular traffic","role":"subject"},{"id":"s6","text":"must not enter the intersection","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s7","text":"when the red signal is exhibited.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal, 'a signal head; state ∈ {circular_green, circular_yellow, circular_red, ...}; several states may be displayed at once': a steady yellow signal alone is circular_yellow and no other state (not flashing_yellow, a flashing indication, and no arrow beside it). Same atom as the index for the signal words of NRS_484B_307_2a."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Vehicular traffic': the admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle ('every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway'), claimed as ru.aggregate, never expanded. 'facing the signal': the subject occupies (rel.occupies) a travel region c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters; st.intersection) and which the head governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls'). Not a stand-in: dev.governs is not a position, st.lane_enters not presence in i. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s5","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'such vehicular traffic' refers back to s2: the same admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, the traffic that faced the yellow."},{"span":"s6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'enter the intersection': the subject's footprint comes to overlap (rel.occupies, 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region') intersection i (st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet'), having not overlapped it at the previous observation. Not a stand-in: st.intersection is not the crosswalk or the stop line. As the index maps 'shall not enter or proceed through an intersection' (NRS_484B_270_4)."},{"span":"s7","atoms":["dev.governs","dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"'when the red signal is exhibited': at the observation of the entry the head s that governs c (dev.governs) displays the steady red indication the yellow announced (dev.traffic_signal state circular_red), with no green arrow and no flashing yellow arrow beside it (narrowing on s6)."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"s3","why":"The words state what the steady yellow indication tells the traffic facing it. They impose no duty and set no condition of the duty in s6, which the rule carries in full."}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, of the classes traffic and vehicle, occupies at the judged observation, or occupied at the previous one, a travel region c whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters) and which a traffic signal head s governs (dev.governs); and s displayed a steady yellow alone (circular_yellow, no other state) at some observation since the subject has occupied c without interruption: it faced the yellow on this approach.","obligation":"The subject does not enter i while the red is exhibited: it is not the case that its footprint overlaps i at the judged observation, did not overlap i at the previous observation, and s displays circular_red at the judged observation with no green arrow and no flashing yellow arrow.","params":[],"narrowings":[{"span":"s6","why":"'the red signal' is read as the steady red indication the yellow precedes (circular_red). Where s displays a green arrow or a flashing yellow arrow beside the red, an entry for that arrow's movement is the arrow's signal (paragraphs 4 and 7), and this duty is not read on it.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car occupies lane c, which enters i and is governed by head s; s displays circular_yellow alone while the car is 30 m short of i at 14 m/s; s changes to circular_red alone 3 s later, and the car's footprint comes to overlap i 0.5 s after the red appears."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same yellow; the car's footprint comes to overlap i while s still displays circular_yellow alone."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"s displays circular_green alone at every observation while the car occupies c; the car enters i."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source does not record which intersection lane c enters: whether the car faces a signal of this intersection is unknown.","masked":["st.lane_enters"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_7a_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-7a"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"Where the signal is a flashing yellow turn arrow, displayed alone or in combination with another signal:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s2","text":"Vehicular traffic facing the signal","role":"subject"},{"id":"s3","text":"is permitted to cautiously","role":"standard"},{"id":"s4","text":"enter the intersection only to make the movement indicated by the arrow signal,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s5","text":"or other such movement as is permitted by other signal indications displayed at the same time.","role":"exception"},{"id":"s6","text":"Such vehicular traffic","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s7","text":"must yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s8","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s9","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within the intersection or an adjacent crosswalk","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s10","text":"and yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s11","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s12","text":"to other traffic lawfully within the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal, 'a signal head; state ∈ {..., flashing_yellow_arrow(dir), ...} with dir ∈ {left, right, straight, u_turn}; several states may be displayed at once': a flashing yellow turn arrow is flashing_yellow_arrow with direction left, right or u_turn; 'displayed alone or in combination with another signal': whatever other states the head displays with it."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Vehicular traffic': the admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle ('every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway'), claimed as ru.aggregate, never expanded. 'facing the signal': the subject occupies (rel.occupies) a travel region c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters; st.intersection) and which the head governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls'). Not a stand-in: dev.governs is not a position, st.lane_enters not presence in i. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s4","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal","rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":["drv.motion.left_turn_through_region","drv.motion.right_turn_through_region","drv.motion.u_turn_through_region"],"justification":"'enter the intersection': the passage through intersection i (st.intersection) from the entry (rel.occupies rising) to the exit. 'only to make the movement indicated by the arrow signal': the movement made, recognized at the exit, is a left turn (drv.motion.left_turn_through_region, 'a turn to the left through region r'), a right turn (drv.motion.right_turn_through_region), a reversal (drv.motion.u_turn_through_region, 'turned so as to proceed in the opposite direction through region r'), or straight through where none of them holds; it must be the movement the flashing yellow arrow's direction (dev.traffic_signal) indicates: a left arrow the turn to the left and the U-turn, a right arrow the right turn, a u_turn arrow the U-turn. As the index maps the arrow movements of NRS_484B_307_4a_o1."},{"span":"s5","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"'other signal indications displayed at the same time': the other states dev.traffic_signal displays ('several states may be displayed at once') at the same observation as the flashing yellow turn arrow. A movement they permit: circular_green, circular_yellow or flashing_yellow permit every movement; a green, yellow or flashing yellow arrow permits the movement of its direction (left: the left turn and the U-turn; right: the right turn; u_turn: the U-turn; straight: the straight movement)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s3","standard":"cautiously (the manner of the permitted entry)","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","kin.speed"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: an entry is cautious where, at the observation of the entry, while the subject's speed is above the halt tolerance, no other road user's centre has a closest approach to the subject's centre, under constant velocities, within the time-to-collision horizon (p.conflict_horizon) at a centre distance below the conflict clearance (p.conflict_centre_clearance)","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, of the classes traffic and vehicle, has entered intersection i from a travel region c whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters) and which a traffic signal head s governs (dev.governs): at the act's onset its footprint came to overlap i, having occupied c and not i at the observation before. At some observation of the passage, from that entry to the judged observation, s displayed a flashing yellow turn arrow (flashing_yellow_arrow with direction left, right or u_turn), alone or with other states. The rule is judged at the passage's recognition: the observation at which the subject's footprint does not overlap i, having overlapped it at the previous observation. The duty does not apply where, at such an observation of the passage at which s displayed the flashing yellow turn arrow, another state s displayed at the same observation permits the movement made (exception s5).","obligation":"At the recognition the movement made through i — a left turn, a right turn or a U-turn where drv.motion.left_turn_through_region, drv.motion.right_turn_through_region or drv.motion.u_turn_through_region holds for the subject and i (step = p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph, turn_min = p.turn_heading_min, u_turn_min = p.u_turn_heading_min), straight through where none holds — is the movement indicated by a flashing yellow turn arrow s displayed at an observation of the passage (left: the left turn or the U-turn; right: the right turn; u_turn: the U-turn); and the entry was cautious: at the entry observation, while the subject's speed was above p.halt_speed_tolerance, no other road user's closest approach to it (prim.closest_approach_within over p.conflict_horizon) was at a centre distance below p.conflict_centre_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance).","params":["p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph","p.turn_heading_min","p.u_turn_heading_min","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s4","why":"The movement is read from the passage through the intersection, recognized at the exit: a left turn, a right turn or a reversal by the turn concepts, straight through where none holds (a heading change below p.turn_heading_min). A left arrow is read as indicating the U-turn as well as the left turn, a U-turn being a turn to the left carried on.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"s3","why":"'cautiously' names no factor; it is read only through the absence of a traffic conflict with any road user at the observation of entry, the time the words fix it to ('cautiously enter').","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Head s governing lane c, which enters i, displays circular_red with flashing_yellow_arrow(left) throughout; the car enters i with no other road user near and passes straight through, heading change 1 degree."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same signal; the car enters i at 6 m/s with no other road user in the scene and turns left, heading change +88 degrees."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"s displays circular_green alone from before the entry until after the exit; the car passes straight through i."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source supplies no yaw rate for the car inside i: the movement made is unknown.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]},{"name":"occasion_s1","expected":"violated","narrative":"s displays circular_red with flashing_yellow_arrow(left) at the car's entry and changes to circular_red with red_arrow(left) while the car is inside i; the car passes straight through: the flashing arrow was displayed for part of the passage only."},{"name":"occasion_s1_outside","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"s displays flashing_yellow_arrow(left) only while the car waits on c; from the entry to the exit it displays circular_green alone; the car passes straight through."},{"name":"occasion_s5","expected":"compliant","narrative":"s displays flashing_yellow_arrow(left) throughout the passage, with circular_green at the entry and circular_red from midway; the car passes straight through: the circular green, displayed with the arrow for part of the passage, permits the straight movement."},{"name":"occasion_s5_outside","expected":"violated","narrative":"s displays flashing_yellow_arrow(left) with circular_green only while the car waits on c; from the entry on it displays flashing_yellow_arrow(left) with circular_red; the car passes straight through."},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"s displays circular_red with flashing_yellow_arrow(left); the car turns left but enters i at 10 m/s while an oncoming car 15 m away at 12 m/s closes on it, the closest approach of their centres 0.7 s ahead at 1 m: the entry was not cautious."}],"occasion":{"act":["drv.motion.left_turn_through_region","drv.motion.right_turn_through_region","drv.motion.u_turn_through_region"],"boundary":"