l': the subject occupies (rel.occupies) a travel region c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters; st.intersection) and which the head governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls'). Not a stand-in: dev.governs is not a position, st.lane_enters not presence in i. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s6","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Such vehicular traffic' refers back to s2: the same admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle."},{"span":"s7","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.contact"],"derived":[],"justification":"'must yield': kin.speed ('magnitude of velocity') tells a subject that moves on toward the pedestrian from one that holds back, and rel.contact ('the bodies of two road users ... touch or overlap (a collision)') is the crash precedence exists to avoid; not a stand-in for a near miss, which the operationalization of s8 reads. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s9","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'pedestrians': the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian. 'within the intersection or an adjacent crosswalk': the pedestrian's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) intersection i (st.intersection) or a crosswalk (st.crosswalk) recorded as marking the entrance (st.entrance_of, 'the carrier whose entrance into an intersection a stop line or a crosswalk marks') of a travel region (st.travel_region) that enters i (st.lane_enters). Not a stand-in: st.entrance_of is the recorded association, never a distance. As the index maps 'lawfully within the adjacent crosswalk' (NRS_484B_307_4a_o2)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s8","standard":"the right-of-way: DEF-NRS-484A-210, 'the right of one vehicle or pedestrian to proceed in a lawful manner in preference to another vehicle or pedestrian approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other'","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","kin.speed"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: the danger of a crash is a closest approach of the two centres, under constant velocities, within the time-to-collision horizon (p.conflict_horizon) at a centre distance below the conflict clearance (p.conflict_centre_clearance); the subject grants precedence where, while its speed is above the halt tolerance (p.halt_speed_tolerance), no such approach to the pedestrian arises. Direction, speed and proximity enter by degree through the constant-velocity extrapolation of both road users.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, of the classes traffic and vehicle, faces traffic signal head s showing a flashing yellow turn arrow: either it occupies a travel region c whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters) and which s governs (dev.governs), and s displays flashing_yellow_arrow with direction left, right or u_turn (with or without other states) at the judged observation; or it occupies i, has occupied it at every observation since it entered i from such a c, and s displayed such an arrow at that entry.","obligation":"For every road user p other than the subject that is of the class pedestrian and whose footprint overlaps i or a crosswalk recorded as marking the entrance of a travel region that enters i at the judged observation: it is not the case that the subject's speed is above p.halt_speed_tolerance while the closest approach of the two centres lies within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) at a centre distance below p.conflict_centre_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance); and the subject's body does not touch p's (rel.contact).","params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s7","why":"'lawfully within' is read through the pedestrian's presence within the intersection or an adjacent crosswalk; whether its presence there is lawful is not judged, so the subject yields to every such pedestrian.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Head s governing left-turn lane c displays circular_red with flashing_yellow_arrow(left); a pedestrian walks at 1.3 m/s in the crosswalk marking the entrance of the cross street's approach into i; the car enters i and turns left at 7 m/s toward that crosswalk, the closest approach of their centres 1.1 s ahead at 0.8 m."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same signal; no other road user is in the scene; the car turns left through i. The duty binds the subject alone and is met."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"s displays circular_green alone; the car turns left past a pedestrian."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source does not record which carriers' entrances the pedestrian's crosswalk marks: whether it is an adjacent crosswalk is unknown.","masked":["st.entrance_of"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_7a_o3","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-7a"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"Where the signal is a flashing yellow turn arrow, displayed alone or in combination with another signal:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s2","text":"Vehicular traffic facing the signal","role":"subject"},{"id":"s3","text":"is permitted to cautiously","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s4","text":"enter the intersection only to make the movement indicated by the arrow signal,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s5","text":"or other such movement as is permitted by other signal indications displayed at the same time.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s6","text":"Such vehicular traffic","role":"subject"},{"id":"s7","text":"must yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s8","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s9","text":"to pedestrians lawfully within the intersection or an adjacent crosswalk","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s10","text":"and yield","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s11","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"s12","text":"to other traffic lawfully within the intersection.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal, 'a signal head; state ∈ {..., flashing_yellow_arrow(dir), ...}; several states may be displayed at once': a flashing yellow turn arrow is flashing_yellow_arrow with direction left, right or u_turn, with whatever other states the head displays ('alone or in combination with another signal')."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Vehicular traffic': the admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed as ru.aggregate, never expanded. 'facing the signal': the subject occupies (rel.occupies) a travel region c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters; st.intersection) and which the head governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls'). Not a stand-in: dev.governs is not a position, st.lane_enters not presence in i. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s6","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Such vehicular traffic' refers back to s2: the same admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle."},{"span":"s10","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.contact"],"derived":[],"justification":"'yield': kin.speed ('magnitude of velocity') tells a subject that moves on toward the other road user from one that holds back, and rel.contact ('the bodies of two road users ... touch or overlap (a collision)') is the crash precedence exists to avoid; not a stand-in for a near miss, which the operationalization of s11 reads. As the index maps 'must yield' (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s12","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'other traffic': road users of the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic ('pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances ... using any highway for purposes of travel') other than the subject. 'within the intersection': its footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) intersection i (st.intersection). As the index maps 'lawfully using the intersection.' (NRS_484B_307_4a_o2)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s11","standard":"the right-of-way: DEF-NRS-484A-210, 'the right of one vehicle or pedestrian to proceed in a lawful manner in preference to another vehicle or pedestrian approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other'","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","kin.speed"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: the danger of a crash is a closest approach of the two centres, under constant velocities, within the time-to-collision horizon (p.conflict_horizon) at a centre distance below the conflict clearance (p.conflict_centre_clearance); the subject grants precedence where, while its speed is above the halt tolerance (p.halt_speed_tolerance), no such approach to the other road user arises. Direction, speed and proximity enter by degree through the constant-velocity extrapolation of both road users.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, of the classes traffic and vehicle, faces traffic signal head s showing a flashing yellow turn arrow: either it occupies a travel region c whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters) and which s governs (dev.governs), and s displays flashing_yellow_arrow with direction left, right or u_turn (with or without other states) at the judged observation; or it occupies i, has occupied it at every observation since it entered i from such a c, and s displayed such an arrow at that entry.","obligation":"For every road user p other than the subject that is of the class traffic and whose footprint overlaps i at the judged observation: it is not the case that the subject's speed is above p.halt_speed_tolerance while the closest approach of the two centres lies within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) at a centre distance below p.conflict_centre_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance); and the subject's body does not touch p's (rel.contact).","params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s10","why":"'lawfully within the intersection' is read through the other road user's presence within the intersection; whether its presence there is lawful is not judged, so the subject yields to every such road user.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Head s governing left-turn lane c displays circular_green with flashing_yellow_arrow(left); an oncoming car already inside i proceeds straight at 11 m/s; the car turns left across its path at 6 m/s, the closest approach of their centres 0.9 s ahead at 1.2 m."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same signal; no other road user is in the scene; the car turns left through i. The duty binds the subject alone and is met."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"s displays green_arrow(left) alone; the car turns left past an oncoming car."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source supplies no velocity-derived speed for the turning car: whether it moved on toward the oncoming car is unknown.","masked":["kin.speed"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_8d","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-8d"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red signal alone:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s2","text":"After complying with","role":"condition"},{"id":"s3","text":"the requirement to stop,","role":"reference"},{"id":"s4","text":"a person driving a motorcycle, moped or trimobile or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"s5","text":"may proceed straight through or turn right or left","role":"condition"},{"id":"s6","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"s7","text":"(1) The person waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device","role":"condition"},{"id":"s8","text":"and the signal does not change","role":"condition"},{"id":"s9","text":"because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"condition"},{"id":"s10","text":"(2) No other device at the place prohibits","role":"condition"},{"id":"s11","text":"either or both such turns, if applicable;","role":"condition"},{"id":"s12","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"s13","text":"(3) The person yields","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s14","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"s15","text":"to pedestrians and other traffic proceeding as directed by the signal at the intersection.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal, 'a signal head; state ∈ {circular_green, circular_yellow, circular_red, ...}; several states may be displayed at once': a steady red signal alone is circular_red and no other state (not flashing_red, and no arrow beside it). The head s is the one governing the rider's approach carrier (s7). Same atom as the index for the signal words of NRS_484B_307_2a."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["prim.region_offset_along","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.intersection","st.lane_direction","st.region_geometry","st.stop_line"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"'After complying with the requirement to stop' requires the halt itself (rule 5), with every qualification of the requirement it names, borrowed from NRS-484B-307-8a (reference s3): 'must stop before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made, or in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, then before entering the intersection'. A stop required is DEF-NRS-484A-255, 'complete cessation from movement': drv.motion.complete_halt. The place: the stop line (st.stop_line, 'the transverse line marking where vehicles halt for a device') recorded as marking the entrance of the rider's carrier c (st.entrance_of), else the crosswalk (st.crosswalk) marking it, else c's entrance end at the intersection (st.intersection); the footprint not overlapping the region (rel.occupies), on its upstream side along c's designated direction (st.lane_direction, sign of prim.region_offset_along) and within p.stop_point_tolerance of it (st.region_geometry distance), on the approach that ends in this entry, as NRS_484B_307_8a_o1 states the place, zone and history bound. Not compliance with that node, which a composed rule grants where it is not engaged; st.region_geometry is not occupancy.","source_spans":["s3"]},{"span":"s4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregates for the defined words: DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle ('every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels'), DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped ('a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle that is propelled by a small engine'), DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle ('a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride'), DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle and DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter, claimed as ru.aggregate and never expanded. 'trimobile' has no applicable definition and is not an aggregate: it is carried by ru.motorcycle, 'motor vehicle on two or three wheels ridden astride, including three-wheeled variants', the class atom that denotes a three-wheeled motor vehicle; the atom has no stand-in exclusion that applies. 'driving' and 'riding' are read through the road user's controlled motion (narrowing)."},{"span":"s5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'may proceed straight through or turn right or left': the rider's entry into intersection i (st.intersection), its footprint coming to overlap i (rel.occupies) having occupied at the observation before a travel region c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters); every movement through i is admitted. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s7","atoms":["dev.governs","dev.traffic_signal","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the applicable official traffic-control device': the signal installation of the intersection the rider is at, observed through its heads: the traffic signal heads (dev.traffic_signal) that govern (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls') a travel region (st.travel_region) entering i (st.lane_enters; st.intersection); the head s governing c is the rider's own. 'official' (DEF-NRS-484A-145, 'placed or erected by a public authority') is presumed from the head's presence (narrowing). 'waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows': from the latest onset of its halt at the place until its entry into i the rider does not overlap i, and in that interval some head of the installation begins a green indication (circular_green or a green_arrow, the lights or lighted arrows that come on once in each cycle of the installation) at least two times: a count of that head's rising green indications since the halt's onset, against the literal two."},{"span":"s8","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the signal does not change': the rider's head s (dev.traffic_signal) displays the steady red alone (circular_red, no other state) at every observation from the latest onset of the halt to the entry."},{"span":"s10","atoms":["dev.governs","dev.regulatory_sign","st.intersection","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'No other device at the place prohibits': a regulatory sign (dev.regulatory_sign, 'a point regulation by catalogue code', codes no_left_turn and no_right_turn) governing (dev.governs) the rider's carrier c (st.travel_region) or the intersection i (st.intersection). Not a stand-in: 'a prohibition sign is a condition', and it is read as one, not as a manoeuvre. 'official' status is presumed from presence."},{"span":"s11","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":["drv.motion.right_turn_through_region","drv.motion.left_turn_through_region"],"justification":"'either or both such turns, if applicable': the turn the rider makes on this passage through intersection i (st.intersection), from its entry (rel.occupies rising) to its exit, recognized at the exit as a right turn (drv.motion.right_turn_through_region, 'a turn to the right through region r, recognized as it leaves r') or a left turn (drv.motion.left_turn_through_region); 'if applicable': only a turn made brings a prohibition into play, and a straight passage is never prohibited by a turn sign. Read from each observation of the passage at the recognition the passage reaches, so that the condition is decided at the entry where the exit is recorded."},{"span":"s13","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.contact"],"derived":[],"justification":"'yields': kin.speed ('magnitude of velocity') tells a rider that moves on toward the other road user from one that holds back, and rel.contact ('the bodies of two road users ... touch or overlap (a collision)') is the crash precedence exists to avoid; not a stand-in for a near miss, which the operationalization of s14 reads. As the index maps 'must yield' (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s15","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","kin.speed","rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","dev.governs","dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"'pedestrians and other traffic': road users of the admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian and DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic other than the rider. 'proceeding': moving, kin.speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance. 'as directed by the signal at the intersection': it overlaps (rel.occupies) intersection i (st.intersection) or a crosswalk (st.crosswalk) recorded as marking the entrance (st.entrance_of) of a travel region that enters i (st.lane_enters, st.travel_region), or it occupies a travel region c' entering i that is governed (dev.governs) by a head displaying a green indication (dev.traffic_signal: circular_green or green_arrow). Not a stand-in: st.entrance_of is the recorded association, never a distance."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s14","standard":"the right-of-way: DEF-NRS-484A-210, 'the right of one vehicle or pedestrian to proceed in a lawful manner in preference to another vehicle or pedestrian approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other'","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","kin.speed"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: the danger of a crash is a closest approach of the two centres, under constant velocities, within the time-to-collision horizon (p.conflict_horizon) at a centre distance below the conflict clearance (p.conflict_centre_clearance); the rider grants precedence where, while its speed is above the halt tolerance (p.halt_speed_tolerance), no such approach to the other road user arises. Direction, speed and proximity enter by degree through the constant-velocity extrapolation of both road users.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[{"span":"s3","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-307-8a","quote":"must stop before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made, or in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, then before entering the intersection","why":"The words borrow the requirement's place and its order (the crosswalk on the nearest side, or the place a sign or pavement marking indicates, else the intersection's edge) and the meaning of stopping before it. The condition requires that the halt itself occurred there; a composition with NRS_484B_307_8a_o1 would not establish it, since a composed rule counts as complied with where it is not engaged, and this paragraph governs riders whether or not that duty engages them (a bicycle or electric scooter is no vehicle). So the borrowed words are carried by the halt, the place and the approach on s2, and no rule of NRS-484B-307-8a need apply, hold or be complied with."}],"residues":[{"span":"s9","why":"The words give the cause of the unchanged red. A head that keeps its steady red alone through two complete cycles of the installation's other indications while the rider waits at its stop place has not served the rider's approach, which is a malfunction or a failure to detect the rider; the duty is the same whichever of the two causes holds, and neither shows in the scene beyond the unchanged red (s8) and the cycles (s7), which the rule reads.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"The subject is of one of the classes motorcycle, moped, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter (admitted aggregates) or a ru.motorcycle (the trimobile). It approached intersection i through a travel region c whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters) and which a traffic signal head s governs (dev.governs), and halted (drv.motion.complete_halt, p.halt_speed_tolerance) at the place of the stop on that approach: the stop line recorded as marking c's entrance, else the crosswalk recorded as marking it, else c's entrance end at i, with the zone (p.stop_point_tolerance) and the history bound NRS_484B_307_8a_o1 states. From the latest onset of that halt until its entry into i, s displayed a steady red alone (circular_red, no other state) at every observation and the subject's footprint did not overlap i; in that interval some traffic signal head governing a travel region that enters i began a green indication (circular_green or a green_arrow rising) at least two times (literal 2). The subject then entered i (its footprint came to overlap i, having occupied c at the observation before) while s still displayed the steady red alone, and its footprint has overlapped i at every observation since that entry, the judged one included. It is not the case that the passage through i begun at that entry is recognized at its exit (at the judged observation or a later one: the observation at which the subject's footprint ceases to overlap i) as a right turn (drv.motion.right_turn_through_region; step = p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph, turn_min = p.turn_heading_min, u_turn_min = p.u_turn_heading_min) while a regulatory sign coded no_right_turn governs c or i, nor as a left turn (drv.motion.left_turn_through_region) while one coded no_left_turn governs c or i; where no such sign governs, this condition holds whatever the movement, and where one governs and the exit is not recorded, it is unknown.","obligation":"For every road user p other than the subject that is of the class pedestrian or of the class traffic and is proceeding as directed by the signal at i — its speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance, and either its footprint overlaps i or a crosswalk recorded as marking the entrance of a travel region that enters i, or it occupies a travel region c' entering i governed by a head that displays circular_green or a green_arrow: it is not the case that the subject's speed is above p.halt_speed_tolerance while the closest approach of the two centres lies within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) at a centre distance below p.conflict_centre_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance); and the subject's body does not touch p's (rel.contact).","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph","p.turn_heading_min","p.u_turn_heading_min"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s4","why":"'driving' and 'riding' are read through the road user's controlled motion, whoever or whatever is at its controls.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"s7","why":"'official' traffic-control device: the presence of the signal heads at the intersection is the evidence of their official status.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"s13","why":"'proceeding as directed by the signal at the intersection' is read through the signal state governing the other road user's approach (a green indication) where it approaches, and through its presence within the intersection or an adjacent crosswalk where it is there; a road user that entered against its own red and is now within the intersection is yielded to as well.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A moped halts 1 m short of the stop line marking lane c's entrance while head s displays circular_red alone; while it waits, the head governing the cross street's lane begins circular_green twice and s stays circular_red alone; no turn-prohibiting sign governs c or i. The moped enters i straight through at 5 m/s while a pedestrian walks at 1.3 m/s in the crosswalk marking the entrance of the far approach, the closest approach of their centres 1.0 s ahead at 0.6 m."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same wait and entry with no other road user in the scene: the duty binds the rider alone and is met."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The moped halts at the line and enters i after the cross street's head has begun circular_green only once since its halt: the wait of two cycles is not met."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source does not observe which travel regions the heads govern: which head is the rider's and whether the cross head belongs to this intersection are unknown.","masked":["dev.governs"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A passenger car (DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, not of the classes of s4) waits two cycles at the line under circular_red alone and enters i."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"As forbid, but the moped halted 15 m short of the line behind a queue and, when the queue cleared, rolled to the line and into i without halting at the place: the halt the requirement to stop names did not occur, and the paragraph does not apply."},{"name":"branch_3","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"As forbid, but a regulatory sign coded no_right_turn governs lane c and the moped's passage through i is recognized at its exit as a right turn (heading change -85 degrees): a device at the place prohibits the turn it made, and the permission with its yield does not arise."}],"literals":[{"span":"s7","text":"two","value":2,"unit":"count"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.turn_heading_min","unit":"deg","value":45.0,"convention":"the smallest heading change over the turn window at which a change of course counts as a turn rather than a lane change or a drift","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_40_080_o1; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.u_turn_heading_min","unit":"deg","value":135.0,"convention":"the smallest heading change magnitude over the turn window at which a turn counts as a reversal of direction","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_40_080_o1; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"the body-to-mark gap within which a halt counts as at the mark: a stop line's set-back before a crossing plus a placement margin","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_20_060_o1; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_8b","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-8b"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red signal alone:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s2","text":"Pedestrians","role":"subject"},{"id":"s3","text":"facing such a signal","role":"condition"},{"id":"s4","text":"shall not enter the highway,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s5","text":"unless permitted to proceed by another device as provided in NRS 484B.283 [NRS-484B-283-1d1, NRS-484B-283-1d2, NRS-484B-283-1d3, NRS-484B-283-1d4].","role":"reference"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal, 'a signal head; state ∈ {circular_green, circular_yellow, circular_red, ...}; several states may be displayed at once': a steady red signal alone is circular_red and no other state (not flashing_red, and no arrow beside it). Same atom as the index for the signal words of NRS_484B_307_2a."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"The admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian ('a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair, or a person on an electric personal assistive mobility device'), claimed as ru.aggregate and never replaced by the class atom ru.pedestrian."},{"span":"s3","atoms":["dev.position","kin.heading","kin.position"],"derived":[],"justification":"'facing such a signal': the head of s1, at its position (dev.position, 'location of the device head / sign face'), lies within p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_reach of the pedestrian's position (kin.position), and the pedestrian's heading (kin.heading, 'direction the body points') makes with the line from its position to the head an angle whose cosine is at least p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_cos. Not a stand-in: dev.position is the place of the head only, never a stop line or crossing. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2b)."},{"span":"s4","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"'shall not enter': the pedestrian's footprint comes to overlap (rel.occupies, 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region') a roadway (st.roadway, 'the part of a highway improved for vehicular traffic, excluding shoulder'), having overlapped none at the previous observation. 'the highway' (DEF-NRS-484A-095, 'the entire width between the boundary lines of every way') is read as its roadway: the pedestrian who faces the head from the sidewalk or the curb already lies within that width, so the entry the words forbid is the step onto the part the signal controls (narrowing on s4); st.roadway's exclusion ('Not a stand-in for: the sidewalk') is the distinction wanted. The same reading as the index gives 'may not proceed to cross the highway' (NRS_484B_283_1d3_o1)."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[{"span":"s5","rule":"NRS_484B_283_1d1","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"s5","rule":"NRS_484B_283_1d2","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"s5","rule":"NRS_484B_283_1d3_o2","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"s5","rule":"NRS_484B_283_1d4_o2","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a pedestrian (DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian). At the judged observation it faces a traffic signal head s: s's position (dev.position) lies within p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_reach of the subject's position (kin.position), and the cosine of the angle between the subject's heading (kin.heading) and the line from its position to s is at least p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_cos; s displays a steady red alone (circular_red, no other state); and at the previous observation the subject's footprint overlapped no roadway. The duty does not apply where NRS_484B_283_1d1 or NRS_484B_283_1d2 applies to the subject (a pedestrian signal permits it to proceed across), nor where NRS_484B_283_1d3_o2 or NRS_484B_283_1d4_o2 applies (a pedestrian who entered lawfully continuing to cross).","obligation":"At the judged observation the subject's footprint overlaps no roadway (rel.occupies, st.roadway): it does not step from the sidewalk, curb or other place off the roadway onto the roadway while it faces the steady red alone.","params":["p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_cos","p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s4","why":"'enter the highway' is read as coming onto the roadway. The highway's defined extent includes the sidewalk, on which a pedestrian facing the head already stands, so read literally the words would never be engaged by the pedestrians they address; the entry they forbid is the step onto the vehicular part the signal controls. Entry onto a shoulder or verge alone is not read as entry.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A pedestrian stands on the sidewalk at a corner, 25 m from a vehicular head it faces (heading within 10 degrees of the line to the head) that displays circular_red alone; the pedestrian head it faces displays dont_walk_steady. At the next observation its footprint overlaps the roadway."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; the pedestrian stays on the sidewalk while the head displays circular_red alone."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The head the pedestrian faces displays circular_green alone; it steps onto the roadway."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source supplies no heading for the pedestrian: whether it faces the head is unknown.","masked":["kin.heading"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"As forbid, but the pedestrian head it faces displays walk: NRS_484B_283_1d1 applies to it and the duty of this paragraph does not."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.87,"convention":"cosine of the largest angle (about thirty degrees) between a pedestrian's heading and the line from its position to a vehicular signal head at which the pedestrian counts as facing that head: the lateral offset of a far-side head from the crossing's line plus a pedestrian's heading wander","source":"proposed this iteration by NRS_484B_307_2b; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.ped_traffic_signal_facing_reach","unit":"m","value":60.0,"convention":"the largest distance from a pedestrian to a vehicular signal head at which the head counts as one the pedestrian faces across the intersection: a wide urban intersection (about 40 m) plus the set-back of a far-side head beyond the far crosswalk","source":"proposed this iteration by NRS_484B_307_2b; repeated unchanged"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_8a_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-8a"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red signal alone:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s2","text":"Vehicular traffic facing the signal","role":"subject"},{"id":"s3","text":"must stop before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made, or in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, then before entering the intersection,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s4","text":"and,","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"s5","text":"except as otherwise provided in paragraphs (c) and (d) [(c) is appended below, NRS-484B-307-8d],","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s6","text":"must remain stopped or standing until the green signal is shown.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s7","text":"After complying with the requirement to stop,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s8","text":"vehicular traffic facing such a signal and situated on the extreme right of the highway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s9","text":"may proceed into the intersection","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s10","text":"for a right turn","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s11","text":"only when the intersecting highway is two-directional or one-way to the right,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s12","text":"or vehicular traffic facing such a signal and situated on the extreme left of a one-way highway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s13","text":"may proceed into the intersection","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s14","text":"for a left turn","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s15","text":"only when the intersecting highway is one-way to the left,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s16","text":"but must yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s17","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s18","text":"to pedestrians and other traffic proceeding as directed by the signal at the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal, 'a signal head; state ∈ {circular_green, circular_yellow, circular_red, ...}; several states may be displayed at once': a steady red signal alone is circular_red and no other state (not flashing_red, and no arrow beside it). Same atom as the index for the signal words of NRS_484B_307_2a."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Vehicular traffic': the admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle ('every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway'), claimed as ru.aggregate, never expanded. 'facing the signal': the subject occupies (rel.occupies) a travel region c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters; st.intersection) and which the head governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls'). Not a stand-in: dev.governs is not the place of the halt, st.lane_enters not presence in i. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s3","atoms":["prim.region_offset_along","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.intersection","st.lane_direction","st.region_geometry","st.stop_line"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"'must stop': a stop required, DEF-NRS-484A-255, '\"Stop,\" when required, means complete cessation from movement': drv.motion.complete_halt. 'before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection': the crosswalk (st.crosswalk, 'marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection') recorded as marking the entrance of the subject's carrier c (st.entrance_of, 'the line or crossing a vehicle approaching through that carrier halts at or before'); 'where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made': the stop line (st.stop_line, 'the transverse line marking where vehicles halt for a device') recorded as marking c's entrance; 'or in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, then before entering the intersection': c's entrance end at intersection i (st.intersection). 'before entering': the footprint does not yet overlap the region (rel.occupies); the side is read by the sign of prim.region_offset_along along c's designated direction (st.lane_direction), the distance to the place by st.region_geometry ('the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it'). Not a stand-in: st.region_geometry is not occupancy, and prim.region_offset_along is read for the side only, never as the distance. Same mapping as the index for the stop words of NRS_484A_450_2 and NRS_484A_450_3."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, of the classes traffic and vehicle, enters intersection i at the judged observation: its footprint overlaps i (rel.occupies) there and did not at the previous observation, at which it occupied a travel region c whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters) and which a traffic signal head s governs (dev.governs); and s displays at the judged observation a steady red alone (circular_red and no other state).","obligation":"Rule 4c duty: an act at a place before an event. Event: the entry into i just described; each such entry is its own occurrence. Place: the stop line recorded as marking c's entrance (st.entrance_of) where one is; else the crosswalk recorded as marking c's entrance; else c's entrance end at the edge of i. Where a mark's association with c is not observed, whether it governs is unknown; where its list of entrances is observed and excludes c, it does not govern and the next place in that order is read. Act: a complete halt (drv.motion.complete_halt, speed_tol = p.halt_speed_tolerance) at an observation at which the subject occupies c, its footprint overlaps neither i nor the crosswalk marking c's entrance and it is not past the stop line where one is the place, it lies on the upstream side of the place along c's designated direction (st.lane_direction; the sign of prim.region_offset_along shows the place ahead, or zero on the line), and its body is within p.stop_point_tolerance of the place (st.region_geometry distance). History bound: the search runs back from the entry and ends at the approach start, the last observation before the entry at which the subject, on c, is outside the place's stopping zone upstream (off the place, short of it, and farther from it than p.stop_point_tolerance), or at the subject's previous entry into i from c, whichever is later; nothing else ends it: not the start of the recording, not the subject's first observation, not another intersection or mark, not a distance travelled. Only an observed exit from the zone upstream begins a new approach; a creep, a lateral move or a change of lane within the zone keeps a halt already made. A halt found: complied. Either end reached without a halt: violated. Neither end reached and no halt found (the recording begins with the subject inside the zone): unknown. Whether the entry occurred is unknown where the observation before does not show the subject on a mapped carrier whose association with the place is observed, or where there is no observation before.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s3","why":"The place 'where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made' is read as the stop line the source records as marking the approach's entrance: a sign standing without a line indicates a place the ontology does not record (no regulatory sign code marks a stopping point), so where only such a sign indicates the place the duty is read at the crosswalk or the intersection's edge. The places are read in the order stop line, crosswalk, edge of the intersection, a halt before the first that marks the approach meeting the words for all of them.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car occupies lane c, recorded as entering i and governed by head s displaying circular_red alone; a stop line marks c's entrance. The car passes the line at 12 m/s, its speed never at or below the halt tolerance, and its footprint comes to overlap i while s still displays circular_red alone; the search from the entry reaches the approach start (the car 40 m short of the line) without a halt."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same approach; the car halts with its body 1 m short of the stop line, footprint off the line and the crosswalk, waits, and then enters i for a right turn while s still displays circular_red alone: the halt lies within the approach."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The car enters i while s displays circular_green alone."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source supplies no speed for the car at any observation of the approach: whether it halted is unknown.","masked":["kin.speed"]},{"name":"history_boundary","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The recording begins with the car already on c with its body 1.5 m short of the stop line, moving at 1 m/s; it enters i under circular_red alone without halting in the recording. The approach start and any earlier entry lie before the recording, so neither end of the search is reached.","boundary":"the car's approach on c before it came within the stop-point tolerance of the stop line"},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"No stop line or crosswalk marks c's entrance (every line's and crosswalk's list of entrances is observed and excludes c); the car halts with its body 1 m short of the edge of i and then enters i under circular_red alone: the place is the intersection's edge."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"the body-to-mark gap within which a halt counts as at the mark: a stop line's set-back before a crossing plus a placement margin","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_20_060_o1; repeated unchanged"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_8a_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-8a"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red signal alone:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s2","text":"Vehicular traffic facing the signal","role":"subject"},{"id":"s3","text":"must stop before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made, or in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, then before entering the intersection,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s4","text":"and,","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"s5","text":"except as otherwise provided in paragraphs (c) and (d) [(c) is appended below, NRS-484B-307-8d],","role":"reference"},{"id":"s6","text":"must remain stopped or standing until the green signal is shown.","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s7","text":"After complying with the requirement to stop,","role":"exception"},{"id":"s8","text":"vehicular traffic facing such a signal and situated on the extreme right of the highway","role":"exception"},{"id":"s9","text":"may proceed into the intersection","role":"exception"},{"id":"s10","text":"for a right turn","role":"exception"},{"id":"s11","text":"only when the intersecting highway is two-directional or one-way to the right,","role":"exception"},{"id":"s12","text":"or vehicular traffic facing such a signal and situated on the extreme left of a one-way highway","role":"exception"},{"id":"s13","text":"may proceed into the intersection","role":"exception"},{"id":"s14","text":"for a left turn","role":"exception"},{"id":"s15","text":"only when the intersecting highway is one-way to the left,","role":"exception"},{"id":"s16","text":"but must yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s17","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s18","text":"to pedestrians and other traffic proceeding as directed by the signal at the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal, 'a signal head; state ∈ {circular_green, circular_yellow, circular_red, ...}; several states may be displayed at once': a steady red signal alone is circular_red and no other state (not flashing_red, and no arrow beside it). Same atom as the index for the signal words of NRS_484B_307_2a."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Vehicular traffic': the admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed as ru.aggregate, never expanded. 'facing the signal': the subject occupies (rel.occupies) a travel region c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters; st.intersection) and which the head governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls'). Not a stand-in: dev.governs is not a position, st.lane_enters not presence in i. Same words, same atoms as the index (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s6","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'remain stopped or standing' (DEF-NRS-484A-255, 'complete cessation from movement'; DEF-NRS-484A-250, 'the halting of a vehicle ... otherwise than for the purpose of and while actually engaged in receiving or discharging passengers') at the place of the stop: the subject's footprint does not come to overlap (rel.occupies) the crosswalk recorded as marking c's entrance (st.crosswalk, st.entrance_of) nor intersection i (st.intersection). 'until the green signal is shown': the duty holds while the head (dev.traffic_signal) displays the steady red alone and ends once it displays another state. Not a stand-in: st.entrance_of is the recorded association, never a distance."},{"span":"s7","atoms":["prim.region_offset_along","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.intersection","st.lane_direction","st.region_geometry","st.stop_line"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"'After complying with the requirement to stop' refers to s3 of this line and requires the halt itself with every qualification s3 states: 'must stop before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made, or in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, then before entering the intersection'. A complete halt (drv.motion.complete_halt; DEF-NRS-484A-255, 'complete cessation from movement') at that place — the stop line (st.stop_line) recorded as marking c's entrance (st.entrance_of), else the crosswalk (st.crosswalk) marking it, else c's entrance end at i (st.intersection) — with the footprint not overlapping the region (rel.occupies), on its upstream side along c's direction (st.lane_direction, sign of prim.region_offset_along) and within p.stop_point_tolerance of it (st.region_geometry), on the approach that ends in this entry: the place, zone and history bound of NRS_484B_307_8a_o1. The halt itself, not compliance with that node, which a composed rule grants where it is not engaged."},{"span":"s8","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency","st.lane_enters"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicular traffic': the admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle. 'facing such a signal': the steady red head governs (dev.governs) the carrier c the subject occupies (rel.occupies), whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters). 'situated on the extreme right of the highway': c is a lane (st.lane, 'a longitudinal strip of roadway for one line of vehicles') whose ordinal equals the count of lanes in its direction (st.lane_adjacency, 'lane ordinal within the carriageway and the count of lanes in that direction; ordinal 1 is the leftmost lane'): the rightmost lane. Not a stand-in: lane membership is read from the ordinal, never from a lateral offset ('lane membership is not an offset from the edge')."},{"span":"s9","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'may proceed into the intersection': the subject's entry into intersection i (st.intersection), its footprint coming to overlap i (rel.occupies) having occupied at the observation before the travel region c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters); the place at which the intention of s10 is declared. As the index maps 'may proceed straight through or turn right or left' (NRS_484B_307_2a)."},{"span":"s11","atoms":["st.highway","st.on_way","st.intersection","st.lane","st.lane_direction","st.median_or_divider"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the intersecting highway': each highway region (st.highway, 'the entire public way between its boundary lines') that i lies on (st.on_way, 'an intersection lies on every way that meets there') other than a highway c lies on. 'two-directional' (DEF-NRS-484B-073, 'an undivided highway upon which vehicles are allowed to proceed in opposite directions'): no median or dividing section (st.median_or_divider, 'physical barrier or dividing section between roadways') lies on it, and two lanes (st.lane) lying on it carry designated directions (st.lane_direction) whose cosine is below minus p.lane_opposed_direction_cos. 'one-way to the right': at least one lane lies on it and every lane lying on it carries a designated direction to the right of c's designated direction, the cross product of c's direction with the lane's (d_x times l_y minus d_y times l_x) being below minus p.cross_direction_sin_min. Not a stand-in: st.on_way is the way a region lies on, not nearness; st.lane_direction is local to its carrier."},{"span":"s12","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency","st.lane_enters","st.one_way_roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicular traffic facing such a signal': as s8. 'situated on the extreme left': c is a lane (st.lane) of ordinal 1 (st.lane_adjacency, 'ordinal 1 is the leftmost lane'); 'of a one-way highway': the subject's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a one-way roadway (st.one_way_roadway, 'roadway on which traffic is restricted to one direction'), as the index maps 'Upon a highway designated and signposted for one-way traffic' (NRS_484B_220_1). Not a stand-in: lane membership is read from the ordinal, never from an offset."},{"span":"s13","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"As s9: the subject's entry into i from c (rel.occupies rising; st.lane_enters; st.travel_region; st.intersection), the place at which the intention of s14 is declared."},{"span":"s15","atoms":["st.highway","st.on_way","st.intersection","st.lane","st.lane_direction"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the intersecting highway': each highway region (st.highway) that i lies on (st.on_way) other than a highway c lies on. 'one-way to the left': at least one lane (st.lane) lies on it and every lane lying on it carries a designated direction (st.lane_direction) to the left of c's designated direction, the cross product of c's direction with the lane's being above p.cross_direction_sin_min. Not a stand-in: st.on_way is not nearness."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[{"span":"s10","id":"int.right_turn"},{"span":"s14","id":"int.left_turn"}],"compositions":[{"span":"s5","rule":"NRS_484B_307_8d","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, of the classes traffic and vehicle, occupies at the judged observation, or occupied at the previous one, a travel region c whose entrance end is intersection i (st.lane_enters) and which a traffic signal head s governs (dev.governs); s displays a steady red alone (circular_red, no other state) at the judged observation; and at the previous observation the subject's footprint overlapped neither i nor a crosswalk recorded as marking c's entrance (st.entrance_of). Exception (paragraph (c), appended in this line, s7 to s15): at the judged observation the subject's footprint overlaps i, it has halted at the place of the stop on this approach (the place, zone and history bound of NRS_484B_307_8a_o1), and either (right) c is a lane whose ordinal equals the count of lanes in its direction, int.right_turn is declared true for the subject at i, and every highway i lies on other than one c lies on is two-directional (no median or divider lies on it; two lanes on it with directions opposed within p.lane_opposed_direction_cos) or one-way to the right (every lane on it points to the right of c's direction by more than p.cross_direction_sin_min); or (left) c is a lane of ordinal 1, the subject's footprint overlaps a one-way roadway, int.left_turn is declared true for the subject at i, and every such highway is one-way to the left. Exception (paragraph (d), s5): NRS_484B_307_8d applies to the subject.","obligation":"At the judged observation the subject's footprint overlaps neither i nor a crosswalk recorded as marking c's entrance (rel.occupies): having stopped, or still short of the place, it remains short of them while the steady red alone is displayed; once s displays another state (the green shown) the duty no longer applies.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance","p.lane_opposed_direction_cos","p.cross_direction_sin_min"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s6","why":"'remain stopped or standing' is read at the place the stop was due: the subject leaves the stop when its footprint comes to overlap the crosswalk marking its carrier's entrance or the intersection while the steady red alone is displayed. A movement short of them, such as closing up behind a vehicle ahead before reaching the place or a creep within the stop-point zone, is not read as leaving the stop: the stop the words require is the one at the place.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car halts at the stop line of lane c (ordinal 2 of 3), which enters i and is governed by head s displaying circular_red alone; int.right_turn is not declared; 5 s later it moves off and its footprint comes to overlap the crosswalk marking c's entrance while s still displays circular_red alone."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The car halts at the line under circular_red alone and stays short of the crosswalk until s displays circular_green; it then enters i."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"s displays circular_green alone throughout the car's approach and entry."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source does not observe which travel regions s governs: whether the car faces s is unknown.","masked":["dev.governs"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The car halts with its body 1 m short of the stop line in the rightmost lane (ordinal 3 of 3), int.right_turn is declared for it at i, and the cross street is undivided with lanes in both directions; it enters i under circular_red alone: paragraph (c)'s exception holds."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"As branch_1, but the cross street is one-way and every lane on it points to the car's left: the exception does not hold, and the entry under the red violates."},{"name":"branch_3","expected":"violated","narrative":"As branch_1, but the car halted 15 m short of the line behind a queue and, when the queue cleared, rolled to the line and into i without halting at the place: the halt the exception refers to did not occur."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"the body-to-mark gap within which a halt counts as at the mark: a stop line's set-back before a crossing plus a placement margin","source":"proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_20_060_o1; repeated unchanged"},{"name":"p.lane_opposed_direction_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.9,"convention":"cosine of the largest angle (about twenty-five degrees) off exactly opposed at which the designated directions of two mapped lanes of one way count as opposite directions of travel: the direction noise of map lane segments along a gently curving way","source":"map lane-direction tolerance, matching the catalogue's tolerance for opposed vehicle headings (p.oncoming_heading_cos)"},{"name":"p.cross_direction_sin_min","unit":"ratio","value":0.5,"convention":"sine of the smallest angle (thirty degrees) by which a way's designated direction lies to one side of an approach's designated direction for that way's traffic to count as flowing to that side: the legs of a junction meet at larger angles, and map direction noise is far smaller","source":"intersection design guidance limiting the skew of junction legs"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
